Maison Balancier — Privacy Policy Last updated: 25 October 2026

Maison Balancier ("the app") is a mechanical desk clock for iPhone, published by Hatice Cigdem Karaca ("we").

The short version: we do not collect, store or share any personal data. The app has no accounts, no ads and no analytics, and it contains no third-party tracking code.

Data stays on your device Your settings (chosen dial, numeral style, second time zone, alarm time and days, night-mode schedule, sound options) are saved only on your device, in the app's own storage. We never receive them. Deleting the app deletes them.

What the app uses, and why

Battery level and charging state: to show the power reserve and wind the mainspring while charging. Read on the device and never stored or sent.
Motion sensors: to move the glare on the crystal when you tilt the device. Processed live on the device, not stored, not sent.
Hinge angle (iPhone Duo): to choose the layout and move the glare. Used on the device only.
Notifications and alarms: to ring your alarm when the app is closed. Alarms are scheduled locally on your device. We run no server and send no push notifications.
Date, time and time zone: to draw the dial and the date window. Used on the device only.
The app does not access your location, contacts, photos, microphone or camera.

Purchases Extra dials are one-time in-app purchases. Payments are processed entirely by Apple through the App Store. We do not receive your name, payment details or Apple ID. We only learn, on your device, which purchases you own. Apple's own privacy policy applies to purchases.

Analytics and crash reports We do not collect any. If you choose to share app analytics or crash data with developers in your iOS settings, Apple may provide us with anonymous, aggregated reports. These contain no personal information.

Children The app is not directed at children and collects no data from anyone, including children.

Changes If this policy changes, we will update the date above and publish the new version at the same address.

Contact Questions: hcigdemkaraca@icloud.com

